1st and 2nd person are not marked for gender


The first or the only element of the possessor fraction of the marker:
- is stressed
- capitalized parts are stressed
- in these examples:
- -EM, EMen, -EPS, EPSen, ETH, ETHen, etc, etc, ad nauseam...

consider writing it in transliterated Jagarôth like so:
- kenetEm, my dog
- thiktâlÔn RorbÔn (see note below) veshotEm ::
- touch.FIN.Unpossessed-singular sun.Unpossessed-singular face.Accusative.1s-possessor
- The Sun touches my face.
- nota bene: thought about it. don't want to do it



Rorbôn :: \-ôn :: a new ending added to things for which the category *possessor* means nothing
\-ôn :: the Unpossesed suffix :: the capitalized *U* is esential
:: Unpossessed :: example :: Rorbôn
thiktâlÔn :: the Unpossessed is also called the Celestial gender
the Celestial gender inheres to things that *shine* only:


suns, moons, stars, planets, fire, meteors, bolides, lightning,
lightning bugs, 

==-ôn== : the Unpossessed/Celelstial Gender marker
: things for which the category *possessor* means nothing
: example :: thiktâlÔn-tat RorbÔn veshotEm ::
: parse :: touch.FIN.Celestial-sg--PAST sun.Celestial-sg face.Accusative.1sg
: translation :: The Sun touched my face.

